Issues.Body:
`ngtsc` now elides imports that are only referenced from the Angular decorators it removes, or from the `emitDecoratorMetadata` types of the declarations those decorate, matching the output of `ngp` (split out from #72174).

Custom `beforeTs` transformers in `NgtscProgram.emit` run ahead of `importPreservingTransformer` so any runtime references they synthesize are preserved. Local compilation, `.d.ts` output, JSX files, and non-Angular decorator metadata are unchanged.

```ts
import {Component, QueryList, ViewChildren} from '@angular/core';

@Component({selector: 'my-cmp', template: ''})
export class MyCmp {
  @ViewChildren('x') items!: QueryList<unknown>;
}
```

Before (under `emitDecoratorMetadata: true`):

```js
import { Component, QueryList, ViewChildren } from '@angular/core';
import * as i0 from "@angular/core";
// ...
```

After:

```js
import { Component, ViewChildren } from '@angular/core';
import * as i0 from "@angular/core";
// ...
```

